import ../../../testing/driver.dl

appearance control appearance:
    padding is 10
    height is 44
    background is UI ink 220 230 240

document disabled test:
    link "Run" to "#" using control appearance
    link "Other" to "#" using control appearance
    text surface "Source" containing "original" using control appearance
    code:
        when the "Run" link is followed:
            set counter to this window's state as a pointer to an integer
            store ((the value at counter) + 1) at counter

set count to 0
set instance to an instance of disabled test with state (the address of count)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 400 by 300 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view the address of view
set the "Run" control in (the address of instance) enabled false
ignore update UI view the address of view
require condition (view's control count = 2) reporting "A disabled command stayed in keyboard traversal"
set layout to view's layout's first
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (layout's painted bounds' x + 10.0) (layout's painted bounds' y + 10.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view the address of view
require condition ((count = 0) and (layout's hover = 0.0)) reporting "A disabled command activated or responded to hover"
activate (layout's node) belonging to (layout's parent) in (the address of instance)
click (layout's node) in (the address of instance)
require condition (count = 0) reporting "A disabled command activated programmatically"
set the "Run" control in (the address of instance) enabled true
activate (layout's node) belonging to (layout's parent) in (the address of instance)
require condition (count = 1) reporting "A disabled command could not be re-enabled"
set the "Source" control in (the address of instance) enabled false
set source to view's layout's first's next's next
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (source's painted bounds' x + 10.0) (source's painted bounds' y + 10.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 4 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "changed" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view the address of view
require condition ((the UI value for (source's node) in (the address of instance))'s text = "original") reporting "A disabled editor accepted input"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Disabled controls skip focus, ignore pointer and programmatic activation, and reject text input."
